; `for` has exactly two shapes and one body expression, and a form that
; is neither is a PARSE error rather than a type error.
;
; `(for i lo hi body)` and `(for x xs body)` are told apart by ARITY,
; because a parser knows no types - three operands after the binder is
; the range, two is the container. That forces the one-body rule: a
; variadic body would make `(for x xs a b)` ambiguous with the range,
; and `{ ... }` is how several expressions are sequenced.
;
; So a fifth element cannot belong to either shape, and the expectation
; string names both rather than only the one the parser happened to be
; attempting. `.axbad` because a parse error stops the file, so this
; case carries exactly one malformed form.
(import IO)

(:: main Int)

(fn (main) (for i 0 5 1 2))
